                            "такой, что невозможно осмотреть целиком; неоглядный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da7401ac-7850-4b84-b506-18c6fd4d5987",
                                "sense_id": "d4aa8fc9-84c7-36cc-850f-54a32e0a9e23",
                                "text": "Днепр расстилался под нами на необозримое пространство ― синий и страшный у берегов, спокойный и серебряный вдали."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b5dee58d-d26f-40de-9493-e29effb09af9",
                        "source_entry_id": "e213520e-0681-3d58-aa33-57cf52b37c86",
                        "source_sense_id": "d4aa8fc9-84c7-36cc-850f-54a32e0a9e23",
                        "target_lang_word": "immense",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "immense",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ef3ec37-b87d-3ed0-9e3a-a5c103f106aa",
                                        "entry_id": "f0eb1e3a-8a7e-3425-8cdb-6949e9a541a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Huge, gigantic, very large."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1b6c134-5640-4579-958b-19a07656048f",
                                                "sense_id": "6ef3ec37-b87d-3ed0-9e3a-a5c103f106aa",
                                                "text": "Then everybody once more knelt, and soon the blessing was pronounced. The choir and the clergy trooped out slowly, […], down the nave to the western door. […] At a seemingly immense distance the surpliced group stopped to say the last prayer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39d04976-b77e-3dd9-8593-60027cf73ff6",
                                        "entry_id": "f0eb1e3a-8a7e-3425-8cdb-6949e9a541a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Supremely good."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "254fd7ff-4a00-33ad-a774-2e568344aad6",
                                        "entry_id": "f0eb1e3a-8a7e-3425-8cdb-6949e9a541a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Major; to a great degree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d221fbf-7788-4d55-a5e7-797678b33649",
                                                "sense_id": "254fd7ff-4a00-33ad-a774-2e568344aad6",
                                                "text": "The gallant young Indian dandies at home on furlough—immense dandies these—chained and moustached—driving in tearing cabs […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "immense",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6aafd14d-6302-3ecf-bf40-9db4f717cf71",
                                        "entry_id": "8b36f04a-4c37-3b74-88ff-388d399eb7ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Immense extent or expanse; immensity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53a5d50e-0d56-48e4-bf61-2b3b90b410be",
                                                "sense_id": "6aafd14d-6302-3ecf-bf40-9db4f717cf71",
                                                "text": "The half of Asia is my prison-house,\nMyriads of convicts lost in its Immense—\nI look with terror to my crowning day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93d99b44-4928-4937-80c8-8245ba1fa958",
                                                "sense_id": "6aafd14d-6302-3ecf-bf40-9db4f717cf71",
                                                "text": "The events that took place in the immenses of the former USSR three years ago remind one about ancient rule of everyday life which is equally applicable both to daily routine and to politics: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "10784e2c-bb14-4de5-a649-97294d4335c4",
                        "source_entry_id": "e213520e-0681-3d58-aa33-57cf52b37c86",
                        "source_sense_id": "d4aa8fc9-84c7-36cc-850f-54a32e0a9e23",
                        "target_lang_word": "vast",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vast",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8749e49b-3435-3695-9788-3b53fc476509",
                                        "entry_id": "ff35927b-8665-38e9-b64a-ae23b58a6df0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very large or wide (literally or figuratively)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1014edba-356b-4e6d-9779-1ab2de5371d0",
                                                "sense_id": "8749e49b-3435-3695-9788-3b53fc476509",
                                                "text": "The Sahara desert is vast."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05e0a350-7fe4-447b-a2eb-2a867b451169",
                                                "sense_id": "8749e49b-3435-3695-9788-3b53fc476509",
                                                "text": "There is a vast difference between them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2512db8f-f9b8-420d-98ba-f467bca440e0",
                                                "sense_id": "8749e49b-3435-3695-9788-3b53fc476509",
                                                "text": "They and the airline itself described an internal process that requires multiple departments to manually redesign the airline’s schedule – a system that works “the vast majority of the time,” Southwest said in a statement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1bf7b01-885e-3ecb-9168-ca8099e041c6",
                                        "entry_id": "ff35927b-8665-38e9-b64a-ae23b58a6df0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very great in size, amount, degree, intensity, or especially extent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03be4272-b6d7-44df-a819-d3e2ccc8a845",
                                                "sense_id": "d1bf7b01-885e-3ecb-9168-ca8099e041c6",
                                                "text": "The exiguity and ſmallneſſe of ſome ſeeds extending to large productions is one of the magnalities of nature, ſomewhat illuſtrating the work of the Creation, and vaſt production from nothing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3272f3f7-45ce-4930-896e-e6ddd96ddb6f",
                                                "sense_id": "d1bf7b01-885e-3ecb-9168-ca8099e041c6",
                                                "text": "Another place where, from the aesthetic point of view, a long tunnel would have been a real blessing, is East London as viewed from the carriage window on the old Great Eastern line. Despite a vast change from crowded slums to tracts of wasteland, due to its grim wartime experience, this approach still provides a shabby and unworthy introduction to the great capital."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e951119-0f4e-4ebe-bbd5-c309807667ec",
                                                "sense_id": "d1bf7b01-885e-3ecb-9168-ca8099e041c6",
                                                "text": "Last spring, the periodical cicadas emerged across eastern North America. Their vast numbers and short above-ground life spans inspired awe and irritation in humans—and made for good meals for birds and small mammals."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "389dd74e-84aa-3f8d-a809-5fe8f5c59586",
                                        "entry_id": "ff35927b-8665-38e9-b64a-ae23b58a6df0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Waste; desert; desolate; lonely."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65af9778-ed3c-490d-afcf-1ca8f509891b",
                                                "sense_id": "389dd74e-84aa-3f8d-a809-5fe8f5c59586",
                                                "text": "the empty, vast, and wandering air"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "vast",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dfc3abc0-3c64-3fbf-a6cd-161dd66fe188",
                                        "entry_id": "f9164684-cb9f-34ae-95b6-dbb88d5c700d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A vast space."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c47ada4-f634-49d7-8ef3-69b3a043c40e",
                                                "sense_id": "dfc3abc0-3c64-3fbf-a6cd-161dd66fe188",
                                                "text": "they have seemed to be together, though absent, shook hands, as over a vast, and embraced, as it were, from the ends of opposed winds."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
